GET simple valide (Host present)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
POST valide avec Content-Length correct
POST /submit HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 13


======
DELETE valide
DELETE /file.txt HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Methode PUT non supportee -> attendu 405
PUT /file.txt HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Methode HEAD non supportee -> attendu 405
HEAD / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Methode inconnue FOOBAR -> attendu 400
FOOBAR / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Methode vide (espace en premiere position) -> attendu 400
 / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Version HTTP/1.1 non acceptee -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: example.com


======
Version HTTP/2.0 non acceptee -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/2.0
Host: example.com


======
Pas de separateur espace dans la request line -> attendu 400
GET/HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Header totalement vide -> attendu 400 (Header empty)

======
Ligne d'en-tete sans deux-points -> attendu 400 (No colon found)
GET / HTTP/1.0
InvalidHeaderLine


======
Pas de CRLF final du tout -> attendu 400 (Empty line in Header)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
======
Content-Length non numerique -> attendu 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: abc


======
Content-Length vide -> attendu 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 


======
Content-Length negatif (signe -) -> attendu 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: -5


======
Content-Length duplique avec la meme valeur -> attendu OK (autorise)
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 10
Content-Length: 10


======
Content-Length duplique avec des valeurs differentes -> attendu 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 10
Content-Length: 20


======
Host absent de la requete -> pas de verif (pas dans la liste des headers connus si absent)
GET / HTTP/1.0
User-Agent: test


======
Host present mais valeur vide -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host:


======
Host duplique -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: a.com
Host: b.com


======
Host valide avec port -> attendu OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com:8080


======
Host = IPv4 valide -> attendu OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 192.168.1.1


======
Host = IPv4 avec port valide -> attendu OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 127.0.0.1:8080


======
Host = IPv4 invalide (octet > 255) -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 300.1.1.1


======
Host = IPv4 reserve 255.255.255.255 -> attendu 400 (exception explicite)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 255.255.255.255


======
Host = IPv6 complet valide entre crochets -> attendu OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:0db8:0000:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001]


======
Host = IPv6 abrege avec :: valide -> attendu OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [::1]


======
Host invalide (espace dans le nom) -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: exa mple.com


======
Nom d'en-tete invalide (espace dans le nom) -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Invalid Name: value


======
Valeur d'en-tete avec caractere de controle invalide -> attendu 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
X-Test: badvalue


======
Target trop long (>8192 caracteres) -> attendu 414
GET  HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Target avec caractere de controle -> attendu 400
GET /bad HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Target relatif (ne commence pas par / ni http://) -> attendu 400
GET relative/path HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
Target absolu avec http:// -> attendu OK (accepte)
GET http://example.com/path HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com

